  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit; the priority is to establish a reliable performance baseline at minimal cost. config_001 (RNA-only, single-profile, PCA n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: it uses a standard linear dimensionality reduction, a single profile, and no learned encoder, making it fast to train and interpret. Running this first gives us a reference accuracy/F1 against which every subsequent design choice (multiprofile aggregation, learned RNA encoders like scVI or scGPT, image modality, and fusion strategy) can be measured for marginal benefit. Because the budget is limited, starting from the cheapest baseline maximizes the number of informative comparisons we can still afford, and it lets us later isolate the effect of each added component (e.g., comparing config_001 vs config_002 to isolate multiprofile+avgpool, or config_001 vs config_016 to isolate adding an image modality with concat fusion) without confounding multiple changes."
